description: Mobile portrait touch context menus use full-screen modals with a selection header.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Mobile context menu → full-screen modal

On **touch mobile portrait** (`useMobileContextMenuMode`), every context menu must open as a **full-screen modal** — not a pointer-anchored Radix popup.

The modal **header** must describe **what was selected** (path, preview text, layer name, cell coords, …).

## Detection

| Module | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `src/hooks/useMobileContextMenuMode.ts` | `portrait && (isMobileLayout \|\| coarse \|\| touch+narrow)` |
| Pass `isMobileLayout` from `App` when the shell already knows mobile layout (sidebar) |

Desktop / landscape: keep Radix `ContextMenu` or anchored `DropdownMenu` at the pointer.

## Shared UI

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `MobileContextMenuModal.tsx` | Full-screen `Dialog` shell, `title` + optional `subtitle`, z-`100010`; wires `useHistoryOverlayBack` so mobile browser back closes the menu without leaving the page |
| `AdaptiveContextMenu.tsx` | `ContextMenu` (desktop) ↔ modal (mobile); `AdaptiveMenuItem` / `AdaptiveMenuSeparator` |
| `mobileContextMenuStyles.ts` | Overlay/panel/item classes, dismiss guard constants |

Prefer **`AdaptiveContextMenu`** for trigger-wrapped menus (cards, layer rows, edit history).

Use **`MobileContextMenuModal` directly** when the menu is opened by coordinates/state (sidebar tree, preview table, cover canvas single modal, table cell menu).

## Header copy

- **Primary (`title`)** — the selected item: file path, message preview, layer label, `N행 M열`, …
- **Subtitle** — context type: `채팅 메시지`, `검색 결과`, `레이어`, `미리보기 표`, …

Never ship a mobile context menu with a generic title only (e.g. just “메뉴”).

## Checklist for new context menus

1. Wire `useMobileContextMenuMode(isMobileLayout?)` (or `AdaptiveContextMenu`).
2. Mobile: `MobileContextMenuModal` or `AdaptiveContextMenu` with meaningful `title` / `subtitle`.
3. Menu actions: `AdaptiveMenuItem` (auto-closes modal) or call `onOpenChange(false)` / `onClose`.
4. z-index: nested portals inside the modal ≥ parent (`z-100010` baseline; see `modal-nested-z-index` rule).
5. Long-press open → `vibrateLongPressAction()` (see `touch-long-press-haptics` rule).
6. Mobile back: use `MobileContextMenuModal` (includes `useHistoryOverlayBack`); optional `historyOverlayId` when stacking with other overlays.

```text
❌ BAD — Radix ContextMenu popup on phone portrait
❌ BAD — mobile modal with no header / generic “옵션” title
❌ BAD — new one-off full-screen menu component instead of MobileContextMenuModal
❌ BAD — context menu modal without history back (back navigates away from the app route)
✅ GOOD — AdaptiveContextMenu + title = message preview, subtitle = “채팅 메시지”
✅ GOOD — SidebarContextMenu mobileDialog + path in header
✅ GOOD — CoverEditor: single MobileContextMenuModal + coverElementLabel(title)
✅ GOOD — browser back closes menu only (`useHistoryOverlayBack` in MobileContextMenuModal)
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
